13
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:22,014
Ten thousand dollars.

14
00:00:22,194 --> 00:00:23,958
The first real milestone.

15
00:00:24,138 --> 00:00:26,677
It's the difference between one bad month

16
00:00:26,677 --> 00:00:27,792
ruining your year,

17
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:29,649
and one bad month being just a

18
00:00:29,649 --> 00:00:30,269
bad month.

19
00:00:30,619 --> 00:00:33,358
Here's why ten thousand matters so much.

20
00:00:33,538 --> 00:00:35,773
With ten thousand dollars saved,

21
00:00:35,773 --> 00:00:38,426
most surprises stop being emergencies.

22
00:00:38,606 --> 00:00:39,647
The car repair,

23
00:00:39,647 --> 00:00:40,550
the vet bill,

24
00:00:40,550 --> 00:00:41,799
the urgent flight.

25
00:00:41,979 --> 00:00:43,279
You stop borrowing.

26
00:00:43,459 --> 00:00:45,396
You stop paying interest on your bad

27
00:00:45,396 --> 00:00:45,665
luck.

28
00:00:45,845 --> 00:00:47,124
And for many people,

29
00:00:47,124 --> 00:00:49,425
it's the first time money feels like

30
00:00:49,425 --> 00:00:51,151
a tool instead of a threat.

31
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:52,330
In this video,

32
00:00:52,330 --> 00:00:54,403
twenty practical ways to get there.

33
00:00:54,583 --> 00:00:55,996
Some help you spend less,

34
00:00:55,996 --> 00:00:57,353
some help you earn more,

35
00:00:57,353 --> 00:00:59,331
and some protect what you've saved.

36
00:00:59,511 --> 00:01:00,742
You don't need all twenty.

37
00:01:00,922 --> 00:01:02,515
Pick five that fit your life,

38
00:01:02,515 --> 00:01:04,218
and you can get to ten thousand

39
00:01:04,218 --> 00:01:05,427
faster than you think.

40
00:01:05,607 --> 00:01:07,520
And we'll look at it from three

41
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:08,754
angles: the numbers,

42
00:01:08,754 --> 00:01:11,222
