68
00:01:58,157 --> 00:02:00,015
This video is education,

69
00:02:00,015 --> 00:02:01,640
not financial advice.

70
00:02:01,990 --> 00:02:02,640
Angle one.

71
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:03,598
The numbers.

72
00:02:03,778 --> 00:02:06,192
Ten thousand dollars sounds like a mountain.

73
00:02:06,372 --> 00:02:07,928
Let's break it into pieces.

74
00:02:08,279 --> 00:02:10,217
Ten thousand dollars in one year is

75
00:02:10,217 --> 00:02:12,544
about eight hundred thirty three dollars a

76
00:02:12,544 --> 00:02:12,876
month.

77
00:02:13,056 --> 00:02:15,084
Or about one hundred ninety two dollars

78
00:02:15,084 --> 00:02:15,448
a week.

79
00:02:15,628 --> 00:02:17,625
Or about twenty seven dollars a day.

80
00:02:17,975 --> 00:02:19,553
Twenty seven dollars a day.

81
00:02:19,733 --> 00:02:20,999
That's a delivery dinner.

82
00:02:21,179 --> 00:02:22,851
A couple of drinks out.

83
00:02:23,031 --> 00:02:24,343
A tank of gas.

84
00:02:24,523 --> 00:02:27,391
Nobody's saying give all of those up

85
00:02:27,391 --> 00:02:28,029
forever.

86
00:02:28,209 --> 00:02:30,594
But it shows that ten thousand dollars

87
00:02:30,594 --> 00:02:31,913
is not one giant act.

88
00:02:32,093 --> 00:02:34,275
It's a few hundred small decisions,

89
00:02:34,275 --> 00:02:35,459
made in your favor.

90
00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:37,474
And if a year is too fast,

91
00:02:37,474 --> 00:02:38,178
stretch it.

92
00:02:38,358 --> 00:02:40,146
Four hundred dollars a month gets you

93
00:02:40,146 --> 00:02:41,353
there in about two years.

94
00:02:41,533 --> 00:02:43,360
Two hundred dollars a month gets you

95
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:45,086
there in a little over four years.

96
00:02:45,266 --> 00:02:47,031
Any of these is a real plan.

97
00:02:47,381 --> 00:02:49,371
Now compare that with where most people

98
00:02:49,371 --> 00:02:49,575
are.

99
00:02:49,755 --> 00:02:52,287
Bankrate's research has found that a large

100
00:02:52,287 --> 00:02:54,639
share of Americans have less than three

101
00:02:54,639 --> 00:02:56,147
months of expenses saved,

102
00:02:56,147 --> 00:02:58,498
and roughly a quarter have no emergency

103
00:02:58,498 --> 00:02:59,403
savings at all.

104
00:02:59,583 --> 00:03:01,851
The Federal Reserve found that about a

105
00:03:01,851 --> 00:03:04,297
third of adults wouldn't cover a surprise

106
00:03:04,297 --> 00:03:06,386
four hundred dollar bill with cash.

107
00:03:06,566 --> 00:03:08,250
So if you reach ten thousand,

108
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:10,049
you'll be ahead of a very large

109
00:03:10,049 --> 00:03:11,210
part of the country.

110
00:03:11,561 --> 00:03:13,708
And here's the hidden math that makes

111
00:03:13,708 --> 00:03:15,740
the first ten thousand so valuable.

112
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,139
If you don't have it,

113
00:03:17,139 --> 00:03:18,997
surprises go on a credit card at

114
00:03:18,997 --> 00:03:20,680
over twenty percent interest.

115
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:23,199
A two thousand dollar emergency,

116
00:03:23,199 --> 00:03:24,368
paid off slowly,

117
00:03:24,368 --> 00:03:26,561
can cost hundreds in interest.

118
00:03:26,741 --> 00:03:28,308
Your savings don't just sit there.

119
00:03:28,488 --> 00:03:30,691
They prevent a cost you would otherwise

120
00:03:30,691 --> 00:03:31,820
pay again and again.

121
00:03:32,171 --> 00:03:34,551
There's one more number worth knowing:

122
00:03:34,551 --> 00:03:35,804
your personal speed.

123
00:03:35,984 --> 00:03:38,290
Take the amount you can realistically save

124
00:03:38,290 --> 00:03:40,650
each month, including the money you'll free

125
00:03:40,650 --> 00:03:42,407
up with the ideas in this video,

126
00:03:42,407 --> 00:03:44,053
and divide ten thousand by it.

127
00:03:44,233 --> 00:03:45,696
That's your number of months.

128
00:03:45,876 --> 00:03:46,712
Write it down.

129
00:03:46,892 --> 00:03:48,128
If it's twelve,

130
00:03:48,128 --> 00:03:48,622
great.

131
00:03:48,802 --> 00:03:49,794
If it's forty,

132
00:03:49,794 --> 00:03:50,927
that's fine too.

133
00:03:51,107 --> 00:03:53,339
A forty month plan you finish beats

134
00:03:53,339 --> 00:03:55,507
a twelve month plan you abandon in

135
00:03:55,507 --> 00:03:55,890
March.

136
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:58,469
And remember that the speed isn't fixed.

137
00:03:58,649 --> 00:04:00,424
Every way you add from this list

138
00:04:00,424 --> 00:04:01,644
shortens the timeline.

139
00:04:01,824 --> 00:04:04,193
A subscription sweep might take a month

140
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:04,436
off.

141
00:04:04,616 --> 00:04:06,706
A paid off car loan might take

142
00:04:06,706 --> 00:04:07,751
six months off.

143
00:04:07,931 --> 00:04:09,742
A raise might take a year off.

144
00:04:09,922 --> 00:04:11,467
The plan you start with is just

145
00:04:11,467 --> 00:04:12,314
your first draft.

146
00:04:12,494 --> 00:04:13,610
Every few months,

147
00:04:13,610 --> 00:04:16,434
recalculate, and watch the finish line move

148
00:04:16,434 --> 00:04:16,894
closer.

149
00:04:17,244 --> 00:04:17,917
Alright.

150
00:04:18,097 --> 00:04:20,118
Twenty ways to get to ten thousand

151
00:04:20,118 --> 00:04:20,593
dollars.

152
00:04:20,773 --> 00:04:22,954
The first five are about setting up

153
00:04:22,954 --> 00:04:25,383
the system, because a good system beats

154
00:04:25,383 --> 00:04:27,066
good intentions every time.

155
00:04:27,416 --> 00:04:28,356
Way number one.

156
00:04:28,536 --> 00:04:29,749
Give the goal a name,

157
00:04:29,749 --> 00:04:30,904
a number and a date.

158
00:04:31,255 --> 00:04:33,042
Saving more is a wish.

159
00:04:33,222 --> 00:04:35,762
Ten thousand dollars by next December is

160
00:04:35,762 --> 00:04:36,206
a plan.

161
00:04:36,386 --> 00:04:38,587
Research on goal setting has found that

162
00:04:38,587 --> 00:04:41,069
specific goals with deadlines lead to better

163
00:04:41,069 --> 00:04:42,423
results than vague ones.

164
00:04:42,603 --> 00:04:43,965
And naming the account,

165
00:04:43,965 --> 00:04:46,452
something like Freedom Fund or Never Broke

166
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:47,636
Again, sounds silly,

167
00:04:47,636 --> 00:04:49,531
but it makes the money feel like

168
00:04:49,531 --> 00:04:50,301
it has a job.

169
00:04:50,651 --> 00:04:52,653
Try this: write the number and the

170
00:04:52,653 --> 00:04:53,949
date on a sticky note,

171
00:04:53,949 --> 00:04:55,716
and put it where you'll see it

172
00:04:55,716 --> 00:04:56,305
every day.

173
00:04:56,485 --> 00:04:58,128
Your bathroom mirror,

174
00:04:58,128 --> 00:05:00,084
your laptop, your fridge.

175
00:05:00,264 --> 00:05:01,476
Every time you see it,

176
00:05:01,476 --> 00:05:03,956
you'll make one or two decisions differently.

177
00:05:04,136 --> 00:05:05,029
Over a year,

178
00:05:05,029 --> 00:05:07,038
that adds up to real money.

179
00:05:07,389 --> 00:05:08,550
Way number two.

180
00:05:08,730 --> 00:05:10,915
Keep your savings in a separate account,

181
00:05:10,915 --> 00:05:12,445
ideally at a different bank.

182
00:05:12,795 --> 00:05:14,605
When your savings sit in the same

183
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:15,757
app as your checking,

184
00:05:15,757 --> 00:05:16,579
they get spent.

185
00:05:16,759 --> 00:05:17,793
Not on purpose.

186
00:05:17,973 --> 00:05:18,875
A little here,

187
00:05:18,875 --> 00:05:19,842
a little there.

188
00:05:20,022 --> 00:05:22,141
Moving them to a different bank adds

189
00:05:22,141 --> 00:05:23,083
a small barrier,

190
00:05:23,083 --> 00:05:24,848
a transfer that takes a day or

191
00:05:24,848 --> 00:05:25,084
two.

192
00:05:25,264 --> 00:05:27,926
That's just enough friction to stop impulse

193
00:05:27,926 --> 00:05:30,156
spending, and not enough to stop you

194
00:05:30,156 --> 00:05:31,394
in a real emergency.

195
00:05:31,744 --> 00:05:34,267
Look for an account that's FDIC insured,

196
00:05:34,267 --> 00:05:36,475
with no monthly fees and no minimum

197
00:05:36,475 --> 00:05:36,980
balance.

198
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,841
And don't connect a debit card to

199
00:05:38,841 --> 00:05:38,994
it.

200
00:05:39,174 --> 00:05:40,959
The goal is a place where money

201
00:05:40,959 --> 00:05:42,859
goes in easily and comes out only

202
00:05:42,859 --> 00:05:44,758
when you really decide it should.

203
00:05:45,109 --> 00:05:46,165
Way number three.

204
00:05:46,345 --> 00:05:47,658
Automate your saving,

205
00:05:47,658 --> 00:05:48,284
on payday.

206
00:05:48,634 --> 00:05:50,868
Most people save what's left at the

207
00:05:50,868 --> 00:05:51,954
end of the month.

208
00:05:52,134 --> 00:05:53,748
And at the end of the month,

209
00:05:53,748 --> 00:05:55,420
there's usually nothing left.

210
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:56,203
Flip it.

211
00:05:56,383 --> 00:05:58,727
Set an automatic transfer for the day

212
00:05:58,727 --> 00:05:59,994
your paycheck lands.

213
00:06:00,174 --> 00:06:02,825
You'll adjust your spending to what remains,

214
00:06:02,825 --> 00:06:04,632
usually without even noticing.

215
00:06:04,812 --> 00:06:07,114
It's the single most powerful habit in

216
00:06:07,114 --> 00:06:08,144
personal finance.

217
00:06:08,495 --> 00:06:10,123
If your employer allows it,

218
00:06:10,123 --> 00:06:12,474
you can even split your direct deposit,

219
00:06:12,474 --> 00:06:14,826
so part of every paycheck goes straight

220
00:06:14,826 --> 00:06:17,298
to your savings account and never touches

221
00:06:17,298 --> 00:06:17,841
checking.

222
00:06:18,021 --> 00:06:20,190
Start with an amount that feels a

223
00:06:20,190 --> 00:06:22,688
little uncomfortable, but not painful.

224
00:06:22,868 --> 00:06:24,667
Then raise it every few months.

225
00:06:25,018 --> 00:06:26,074
Way number four.

226
00:06:26,254 --> 00:06:29,029
Send every windfall straight to savings.

227
00:06:29,379 --> 00:06:31,302
Tax refunds, bonuses,

228
00:06:31,302 --> 00:06:33,500
birthday money, rebates.

229
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:36,726
IRS filing statistics show the average federal

230
00:06:36,726 --> 00:06:39,440
tax refund has been around three thousand

231
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,029
dollars in recent years.

232
00:06:41,209 --> 00:06:42,431
For a lot of people,

233
00:06:42,431 --> 00:06:44,631
that single refund is almost a third

234
00:06:44,631 --> 00:06:46,770
of the way to ten thousand dollars.

235
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:49,633
The trick is deciding before the money

236
00:06:49,633 --> 00:06:50,162
arrives.

237
00:06:50,342 --> 00:06:52,163
Once it's in your checking account,

238
00:06:52,163 --> 00:06:54,139
it starts to feel like spending money.

239
00:06:54,319 --> 00:06:56,584
Decide now: all windfalls go to the

240
00:06:56,584 --> 00:06:56,908
goal.

241
00:06:57,088 --> 00:06:58,520
Or if that's too strict,

242
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,072
try an eighty twenty rule.

243
00:07:00,252 --> 00:07:01,626
Eighty percent saved,

244
00:07:01,626 --> 00:07:03,131
twenty percent enjoyed.

245
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:04,618
Way number five.

246
00:07:04,798 --> 00:07:06,609
Check your progress once a week.

247
00:07:06,959 --> 00:07:08,086
Not obsessively.

248
00:07:08,266 --> 00:07:10,681
Just once, same day every week.

249
00:07:10,861 --> 00:07:12,347
How much is in the account?

250
00:07:12,527 --> 00:07:13,583
How much did you spend?

251
00:07:13,763 --> 00:07:15,961
Seeing the number grow is motivating,

252
00:07:15,961 --> 00:07:17,981
and noticing a bad week early lets

253
00:07:17,981 --> 00:07:19,763
you fix it before it becomes a

254
00:07:19,763 --> 00:07:20,358
bad month.

255
00:07:20,707 --> 00:07:22,779
Some people use a simple chart on

256
00:07:22,779 --> 00:07:24,788
the fridge, with a box for every

257
00:07:24,788 --> 00:07:26,420
two hundred fifty dollars.

258
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:28,573
Fifty boxes to ten thousand.

259
00:07:28,753 --> 00:07:31,563
Coloring in a box feels surprisingly good.

260
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:34,243
It turns saving from something abstract into

261
00:07:34,243 --> 00:07:35,493
something you can see.

262
00:07:35,842 --> 00:07:37,915
Now, the next seven ways are about

263
00:07:37,915 --> 00:07:40,962
spending less, without making your life miserable.

264
00:07:41,313 --> 00:07:42,497
Way number six.

265
00:07:42,677 --> 00:07:44,314
Do a subscription sweep.

266
00:07:44,664 --> 00:07:46,729
Streaming services, apps,

267
00:07:46,729 --> 00:07:50,116
memberships, software, a gym you don't go

268
00:07:50,116 --> 00:07:50,364
to.

269
00:07:50,544 --> 00:07:51,862
Each one is small,

270
00:07:51,862 --> 00:07:53,911
so it slips under the radar.

271
00:07:54,091 --> 00:07:56,397
Together, they can easily add up to

272
00:07:56,397 --> 00:07:58,770
one hundred dollars a month or more.

273
00:07:58,950 --> 00:08:00,525
And many renew automatically,

274
00:08:00,525 --> 00:08:02,318
so you keep paying long after you

275
00:08:02,318 --> 00:08:03,350
stopped using them.

276
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:05,787
Go through the last two months of

277
00:08:05,787 --> 00:08:07,684
your bank and card statements,

278
00:08:07,684 --> 00:08:08,506
line by line.

279
00:08:08,686 --> 00:08:10,874
Cancel anything you didn't use in the

280
00:08:10,874 --> 00:08:11,879
last thirty days.

281
00:08:12,059 --> 00:08:13,847
You can always sign up again later.

282
00:08:14,027 --> 00:08:16,201
Many people find fifty to one hundred

283
00:08:16,201 --> 00:08:17,788
dollars a month in an hour.

284
00:08:17,968 --> 00:08:20,122
That's six hundred to twelve hundred dollars

285
00:08:20,122 --> 00:08:20,465
a year.

286
00:08:20,815 --> 00:08:22,022
Way number seven.

287
00:08:22,202 --> 00:08:23,897
Negotiate your bills.

288
00:08:24,247 --> 00:08:26,861
Phone, internet, car insurance,

289
00:08:26,861 --> 00:08:29,053
home or renters insurance.

290
00:08:29,233 --> 00:08:31,859
Companies often give their best prices to

291
00:08:31,859 --> 00:08:34,805
new customers, which means loyal customers can

292
00:08:34,805 --> 00:08:36,790
end up paying more for the same

293
00:08:36,790 --> 00:08:37,174
thing.

294
00:08:37,354 --> 00:08:38,662
A few phone calls,

295
00:08:38,662 --> 00:08:40,333
or a few online quotes,

296
00:08:40,333 --> 00:08:42,730
can lower these bills noticeably.

297
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:46,108
Try this: get two quotes from competitors

298
00:08:46,108 --> 00:08:46,551
first.

299
00:08:46,731 --> 00:08:48,531
Then call your current provider,

300
00:08:48,531 --> 00:08:50,499
tell them what you've been offered,

301
00:08:50,499 --> 00:08:52,130
and ask if they can match it.

302
00:08:52,310 --> 00:08:53,819
If not, switch.

303
00:08:53,999 --> 00:08:56,347
An hour of calls could save fifty

304
00:08:56,347 --> 00:08:58,979
to one hundred fifty dollars a month,

305
00:08:58,979 --> 00:09:01,612
every month, with zero change in your

306
00:09:01,612 --> 00:09:02,323
lifestyle.

307
00:09:02,674 --> 00:09:03,649
Way number eight.

308
00:09:03,829 --> 00:09:05,582
Cut back on food delivery.

309
00:09:05,932 --> 00:09:08,164
Delivery apps add service fees,

310
00:09:08,164 --> 00:09:11,116
delivery fees, tips and often higher menu

311
00:09:11,116 --> 00:09:11,620
prices.

312
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:14,092
A twenty dollar meal can easily become

313
00:09:14,092 --> 00:09:16,142
thirty dollars or more by the time

314
00:09:16,142 --> 00:09:17,408
it reaches your door.

315
00:09:17,588 --> 00:09:20,398
You're paying a big premium for convenience.

316
00:09:20,748 --> 00:09:21,595
You don't have to quit.

317
00:09:21,775 --> 00:09:23,042
Pick it up yourself,

318
00:09:23,042 --> 00:09:23,992
or set a limit,

319
00:09:23,992 --> 00:09:26,208
like twice a month instead of twice

320
00:09:26,208 --> 00:09:26,651
a week.

321
00:09:26,831 --> 00:09:28,805
Cooking a few simple meals in bulk

322
00:09:28,805 --> 00:09:30,837
on Sunday can cover lunches for the

323
00:09:30,837 --> 00:09:31,127
week.

324
00:09:31,307 --> 00:09:33,153
Small change, real money.

325
00:09:33,333 --> 00:09:35,277
Many households save one hundred to two

326
00:09:35,277 --> 00:09:36,723
hundred dollars a month here.

327
00:09:37,073 --> 00:09:38,245
Way number nine.

328
00:09:38,425 --> 00:09:40,178
Avoid a big car payment.

329
00:09:40,529 --> 00:09:43,278
Edmunds has reported that the average monthly

330
00:09:43,278 --> 00:09:45,049
payment on a new car loan has

331
00:09:45,049 --> 00:09:47,065
been above seven hundred dollars.

332
00:09:47,245 --> 00:09:49,804
That's over eight thousand dollars a year,

333
00:09:49,804 --> 00:09:52,485
almost your entire ten thousand dollar goal,

334
00:09:52,485 --> 00:09:54,374
going to a car that loses value

335
00:09:54,374 --> 00:09:55,105
every month.

336
00:09:55,455 --> 00:09:56,959
If your current car runs,

337
00:09:56,959 --> 00:09:57,440
keep it.

338
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:58,909
If you need a car,

339
00:09:58,909 --> 00:10:00,986
consider a reliable used one,

340
00:10:00,986 --> 00:10:02,705
and keep the loan short.

341
00:10:02,885 --> 00:10:04,752
And when you finally pay off a

342
00:10:04,752 --> 00:10:06,868
car loan, here's the best trick in

343
00:10:06,868 --> 00:10:09,792
personal finance: keep making the same payment,

344
00:10:09,792 --> 00:10:11,535
but to your savings account.

345
00:10:11,715 --> 00:10:14,081
You're already used to living without that

346
00:10:14,081 --> 00:10:14,420
money.

347
00:10:14,770 --> 00:10:15,756
Way number ten.

348
00:10:15,936 --> 00:10:17,794
Rethink your housing costs.

349
00:10:18,144 --> 00:10:20,616
Housing is the biggest expense for most

350
00:10:20,616 --> 00:10:21,313
households.

351
00:10:21,493 --> 00:10:23,113
That makes it the place where a

352
00:10:23,113 --> 00:10:24,628
single change saves the most.

353
00:10:24,808 --> 00:10:27,633
A roommate, a slightly smaller apartment,

354
00:10:27,633 --> 00:10:29,562
or a place a bit further out

355
00:10:29,562 --> 00:10:31,836
can free up hundreds of dollars a

356
00:10:31,836 --> 00:10:32,250
month.

357
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:33,823
It's not for everyone,

358
00:10:33,823 --> 00:10:34,991
and it's not forever.

359
00:10:35,171 --> 00:10:37,158
But even one year with a roommate,

360
00:10:37,158 --> 00:10:39,262
saving four hundred dollars a month,

361
00:10:39,262 --> 00:10:41,892
puts nearly five thousand dollars toward your

362
00:10:41,892 --> 00:10:42,184
goal.

363
00:10:42,364 --> 00:10:44,422
Half of your first ten thousand,

364
00:10:44,422 --> 00:10:45,580
from one decision.

365
00:10:45,930 --> 00:10:47,021
Way number eleven.

366
00:10:47,201 --> 00:10:48,699
Sell things you don't use.

367
00:10:49,049 --> 00:10:51,854
Most homes have hundreds or even thousands

368
00:10:51,854 --> 00:10:53,658
of dollars of unused stuff.

369
00:10:53,838 --> 00:10:55,729
Old phones, electronics,

370
00:10:55,729 --> 00:10:58,094
furniture, tools, sports gear,

371
00:10:58,094 --> 00:11:00,537
clothes with the tags still on.

372
00:11:00,717 --> 00:11:03,290
Online marketplaces make it easy to sell

373
00:11:03,290 --> 00:11:03,805
locally.

374
00:11:04,155 --> 00:11:06,602
Try this: walk through your home with

375
00:11:06,602 --> 00:11:06,999
a box.

376
00:11:07,179 --> 00:11:09,219
Anything you haven't used in a year

377
00:11:09,219 --> 00:11:10,151
goes in the box.

378
00:11:10,331 --> 00:11:11,963
Sell what's worth selling,

379
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:12,967
donate the rest.

380
00:11:13,147 --> 00:11:15,341
Every dollar goes straight to savings.

381
00:11:15,521 --> 00:11:17,542
It's one of the fastest ways to

382
00:11:17,542 --> 00:11:19,759
build momentum in the first month.

383
00:11:20,109 --> 00:11:21,235
Way number twelve.

384
00:11:21,415 --> 00:11:23,586
Use a thirty day rule for wants.

385
00:11:23,936 --> 00:11:26,025
When you want something that isn't a

386
00:11:26,025 --> 00:11:27,999
need, write it down with the date,

387
00:11:27,999 --> 00:11:29,218
and wait thirty days.

388
00:11:29,398 --> 00:11:31,404
If you still want it after thirty

389
00:11:31,404 --> 00:11:33,227
days, and it fits your budget,

390
00:11:33,227 --> 00:11:34,321
buy it guilt free.

391
00:11:34,501 --> 00:11:36,681
You'll be surprised how often the urge

392
00:11:36,681 --> 00:11:37,427
simply fades.

393
00:11:37,777 --> 00:11:40,114
This works because a lot of spending

394
00:11:40,114 --> 00:11:40,958
is emotional.

395
00:11:41,138 --> 00:11:41,963
A bad day,

396
00:11:41,963 --> 00:11:42,953
a clever ad,

397
00:11:42,953 --> 00:11:44,272
a friend's post.

398
00:11:44,452 --> 00:11:46,626
The thirty day rule puts time between

399
00:11:46,626 --> 00:11:48,330
the feeling and the purchase.

400
00:11:48,510 --> 00:11:50,325
People who try it often find that

401
00:11:50,325 --> 00:11:52,084
a large share of their wish list

402
00:11:52,084 --> 00:11:53,294
disappears on its own.

403
00:11:53,644 --> 00:11:54,561
Quick pause.

404
00:11:54,741 --> 00:11:56,338
If these ideas are helping,

405
00:11:56,338 --> 00:11:57,817
subscribe to the channel.

406
00:11:57,997 --> 00:12:00,307
Every week I break down another step

407
00:12:00,307 --> 00:12:02,488
on the road from zero to financial

408
00:12:02,488 --> 00:12:05,247
freedom, and subscribing is the easiest way

409
00:12:05,247 --> 00:12:06,659
to keep going with me.

410
00:12:06,839 --> 00:12:08,746
Now, the next five ways are about

411
00:12:08,746 --> 00:12:11,174
earning more, because cutting has a limit,

412
00:12:11,174 --> 00:12:12,330
and earning doesn't.

413
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:13,957
Way number thirteen.

414
00:12:14,137 --> 00:12:15,483
Ask for a raise.

415
00:12:15,834 --> 00:12:17,366
Many people never ask.

416
00:12:17,546 --> 00:12:19,795
But a conversation of thirty minutes can

417
00:12:19,795 --> 00:12:21,874
be worth thousands of dollars a year,

418
00:12:21,874 --> 00:12:23,223
for every year you stay.

419
00:12:23,403 --> 00:12:24,735
And raises compound,

420
00:12:24,735 --> 00:12:27,796
because future raises are usually a percentage

421
00:12:27,796 --> 00:12:29,127
of your current pay.

422
00:12:29,477 --> 00:12:30,069
Prepare.

423
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:32,575
Look up salary data for your role

424
00:12:32,575 --> 00:12:33,209
and city.

425
00:12:33,389 --> 00:12:35,035
Write down what you've achieved,

426
00:12:35,035 --> 00:12:36,269
with numbers if you can.

427
00:12:36,449 --> 00:12:38,283
Then ask for a specific amount.

428
00:12:38,463 --> 00:12:39,621
If the answer is no,

429
00:12:39,621 --> 00:12:41,301
ask what it would take to get

430
00:12:41,301 --> 00:12:42,460
there in six months,

431
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:43,734
and get it in writing.

432
00:12:43,914 --> 00:12:45,768
Send every dollar of the raise to

433
00:12:45,768 --> 00:12:47,734
your goal for the first few months.

434
00:12:48,084 --> 00:12:49,361
Way number fourteen.

435
00:12:49,541 --> 00:12:50,818
Take extra hours,

436
00:12:50,818 --> 00:12:52,246
for a limited time.

437
00:12:52,596 --> 00:12:55,009
If your job offers overtime or extra

438
00:12:55,009 --> 00:12:57,288
shifts, a few months of extra work

439
00:12:57,288 --> 00:12:59,701
can speed up your goal dramatically.

440
00:12:59,881 --> 00:13:01,808
Overtime is often paid at a higher

441
00:13:01,808 --> 00:13:03,905
rate, and it goes straight into money

442
00:13:03,905 --> 00:13:05,605
you're not used to having yet.

443
00:13:05,955 --> 00:13:07,557
The key is a time limit.

444
00:13:07,737 --> 00:13:09,118
Burning out isn't a plan.

445
00:13:09,298 --> 00:13:10,308
Try a sprint:

446
00:13:10,308 --> 00:13:12,484
three months of extra hours,

447
00:13:12,484 --> 00:13:14,815
every extra dollar to savings,

448
00:13:14,815 --> 00:13:16,369
then back to normal.

449
00:13:16,549 --> 00:13:18,362
A short sprint can cover a big

450
00:13:18,362 --> 00:13:20,357
chunk of the way to ten thousand.

451
00:13:20,707 --> 00:13:22,053
Way number fifteen.

452
00:13:22,233 --> 00:13:24,358
Turn a skill into side income.

453
00:13:24,708 --> 00:13:26,811
Tutoring, pet sitting,

454
00:13:26,811 --> 00:13:29,106
handyman work, cleaning,

455
00:13:29,106 --> 00:13:31,879
editing, design, translation,

456
00:13:31,879 --> 00:13:32,835
lawn care.

457
00:13:33,015 --> 00:13:34,592
If you have a skill people pay

458
00:13:34,592 --> 00:13:36,011
for, a few hours a week can

459
00:13:36,011 --> 00:13:37,798
add a few hundred dollars a month.

460
00:13:37,978 --> 00:13:39,534
You don't need a business plan.

461
00:13:39,714 --> 00:13:41,086
You need one customer,

462
00:13:41,086 --> 00:13:41,896
then another.

463
00:13:42,247 --> 00:13:44,569
Start with people who already know you.

464
00:13:44,749 --> 00:13:47,591
Tell friends, family and neighbors what you

465
00:13:47,591 --> 00:13:47,988
offer.

466
00:13:48,168 --> 00:13:49,354
Price it fairly,

467
00:13:49,354 --> 00:13:50,392
do great work,

468
00:13:50,392 --> 00:13:52,022
and ask for referrals.

469
00:13:52,202 --> 00:13:53,754
And remember taxes:

470
00:13:53,754 --> 00:13:56,286
side income is usually taxable,

471
00:13:56,286 --> 00:13:58,573
so set aside a part of every

472
00:13:58,573 --> 00:13:59,226
payment.

473
00:13:59,577 --> 00:14:01,040
Way number sixteen.

474
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:02,973
Consider switching jobs.

475
00:14:03,323 --> 00:14:06,054
Wage tracking by the Federal Reserve Bank

476
00:14:06,054 --> 00:14:08,585
of Atlanta has often shown that people

477
00:14:08,585 --> 00:14:11,049
who change jobs see faster pay growth

478
00:14:11,049 --> 00:14:12,448
than people who stay.

479
00:14:12,628 --> 00:14:13,743
Loyalty is nice,

480
00:14:13,743 --> 00:14:16,111
but the market often pays more for

481
00:14:16,111 --> 00:14:17,226
the same skills.

482
00:14:17,576 --> 00:14:18,690
You don't have to leave.

483
00:14:18,870 --> 00:14:20,356
But you should know what you're worth.

484
00:14:20,536 --> 00:14:21,818
Update your resume,

485
00:14:21,818 --> 00:14:22,965
look at listings,

486
00:14:22,965 --> 00:14:25,191
and talk to one or two recruiters

487
00:14:25,191 --> 00:14:25,865
each year.

488
00:14:26,045 --> 00:14:27,792
Either you find a better offer,

489
00:14:27,792 --> 00:14:29,765
or you get the information you need

490
00:14:29,765 --> 00:14:31,456
to ask for more where you are.

491
00:14:31,806 --> 00:14:33,129
Way number seventeen.

492
00:14:33,309 --> 00:14:35,198
Use cash back the right way,

493
00:14:35,198 --> 00:14:36,142
or not at all.

494
00:14:36,492 --> 00:14:38,679
Cash back cards can give you one

495
00:14:38,679 --> 00:14:40,730
to two percent or more back on

496
00:14:40,730 --> 00:14:41,345
spending.

497
00:14:41,525 --> 00:14:43,177
But only if you pay the full

498
00:14:43,177 --> 00:14:44,358
balance every month.

499
00:14:44,538 --> 00:14:47,028
Carry a balance at over twenty percent

500
00:14:47,028 --> 00:14:49,584
interest, and the rewards are wiped out

501
00:14:49,584 --> 00:14:50,633
many times over.

502
00:14:50,983 --> 00:14:52,397
If you trust yourself,

503
00:14:52,397 --> 00:14:54,518
use one simple cash back card for

504
00:14:54,518 --> 00:14:56,767
normal spending, pay it off in full

505
00:14:56,767 --> 00:14:59,724
automatically, and send the rewards to savings

506
00:14:59,724 --> 00:15:00,816
every few months.

507
00:15:00,996 --> 00:15:03,242
If you don't trust yourself with credit

508
00:15:03,242 --> 00:15:05,199
cards yet, skip this one entirely.

509
00:15:05,379 --> 00:15:06,822
That's a smart decision,

510
00:15:06,822 --> 00:15:07,724
not a weak one.

511
00:15:08,075 --> 00:15:09,990
And the last three ways are about

512
00:15:09,990 --> 00:15:11,442
protecting what you save,

513
00:15:11,442 --> 00:15:13,648
so it keeps growing instead of leaking

514
00:15:13,648 --> 00:15:13,938
away.

515
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:15,565
Way number eighteen.

516
00:15:15,745 --> 00:15:17,788
Stop paying bank fees.

517
00:15:18,138 --> 00:15:21,299
The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau has reported

518
00:15:21,299 --> 00:15:24,042
that overdraft fees have typically been around

519
00:15:24,042 --> 00:15:25,533
thirty five dollars each.

520
00:15:25,713 --> 00:15:26,969
A few overdrafts,

521
00:15:26,969 --> 00:15:29,111
some out of network ATM fees,

522
00:15:29,111 --> 00:15:31,549
and a late payment fee can easily

523
00:15:31,549 --> 00:15:33,986
cost a hundred dollars or more in

524
00:15:33,986 --> 00:15:35,094
a single month.

525
00:15:35,444 --> 00:15:37,952
Turn off overdraft coverage if you can.

526
00:15:38,132 --> 00:15:40,140
Set up low balance alerts.

527
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:42,059
Put every bill on autopay for at

528
00:15:42,059 --> 00:15:43,037
least the minimum.

529
00:15:43,217 --> 00:15:45,399
And use your own bank's ATMs.

530
00:15:45,579 --> 00:15:46,865
These are boring fixes,

531
00:15:46,865 --> 00:15:48,654
but every fee you stop paying is

532
00:15:48,654 --> 00:15:50,667
money that goes to your goal instead

533
00:15:50,667 --> 00:15:51,338
of the bank.

534
00:15:51,688 --> 00:15:52,930
Way number nineteen.

535
00:15:53,110 --> 00:15:54,886
Make your savings earn interest.

536
00:15:55,237 --> 00:15:57,668
Many big banks pay almost nothing on

537
00:15:57,668 --> 00:15:58,209
savings.

538
00:15:58,389 --> 00:16:01,127
Online banks and some credit unions often

539
00:16:01,127 --> 00:16:03,465
pay much more on high yield savings

540
00:16:03,465 --> 00:16:04,066
accounts.

541
00:16:04,246 --> 00:16:06,118
Rates change with the economy,

542
00:16:06,118 --> 00:16:08,489
but the difference can be significant,

543
00:16:08,489 --> 00:16:10,423
and it costs nothing to switch.

544
00:16:10,773 --> 00:16:12,287
On ten thousand dollars,

545
00:16:12,287 --> 00:16:14,810
the difference between almost zero and a

546
00:16:14,810 --> 00:16:16,955
few percent could be a few hundred

547
00:16:16,955 --> 00:16:17,901
dollars a year.

548
00:16:18,081 --> 00:16:19,388
It won't make you rich,

549
00:16:19,388 --> 00:16:21,548
but it's free money for your emergency

550
00:16:21,548 --> 00:16:23,196
fund, and it helps it keep up

551
00:16:23,196 --> 00:16:24,049
with inflation.

552
00:16:24,229 --> 00:16:27,055
Just make sure the account is FDIC

553
00:16:27,055 --> 00:16:28,385
or NCUA insured.

554
00:16:28,735 --> 00:16:29,803
Way number twenty.

555
00:16:29,983 --> 00:16:31,295
Save your raises.

556
00:16:31,645 --> 00:16:33,107
When your income goes up,

557
00:16:33,107 --> 00:16:34,861
your spending usually follows.

558
00:16:35,041 --> 00:16:36,376
That's lifestyle creep.

559
00:16:36,556 --> 00:16:38,494
The easiest way to beat it is

560
00:16:38,494 --> 00:16:39,897
to decide in advance:

561
00:16:39,897 --> 00:16:42,102
at least half of every raise goes

562
00:16:42,102 --> 00:16:42,837
to savings.

563
00:16:43,017 --> 00:16:44,761
Your life still gets better,

564
00:16:44,761 --> 00:16:47,440
and your savings rate climbs automatically.

565
00:16:47,790 --> 00:16:49,812
Say you get a three thousand dollar

566
00:16:49,812 --> 00:16:50,158
raise.

567
00:16:50,338 --> 00:16:52,312
You keep fifteen hundred to enjoy,

568
00:16:52,312 --> 00:16:54,518
and fifteen hundred goes to your goal.

569
00:16:54,698 --> 00:16:56,735
That's one hundred twenty five dollars a

570
00:16:56,735 --> 00:16:58,314
month you never had to cut from

571
00:16:58,314 --> 00:16:58,773
anything.

572
00:16:58,953 --> 00:17:00,608
Do this with every raise,

573
00:17:00,608 --> 00:17:02,595
and you'll reach ten thousand,

574
00:17:02,595 --> 00:17:04,648
and then the next ten thousand,

575
00:17:04,648 --> 00:17:06,105
almost without trying.

576
00:17:06,455 --> 00:17:09,131
Let's make this concrete with three example

